+## 2026-11-06: Wi-Fi toggle failed on 0208; haptics felt weak/long; restored 0209 temporarily
+- USER could not enable Wi-Fi. Live wland firmware log confirms WMI READY + HTT VERSION_CONF + initial scan STARTED, but no terminal scan event and no bridge hello. The bridge gates FW_HELLO/interface publication on radio_scans()>0, so an unfinished first scan can withhold the Wi-Fi interface indefinitely.
+- Targeted restart of native wifid succeeded (new PID), but USER still could not enable Wi-Fi. No saved network settings changed, no wland/ADSP reset performed. This failure is not proof the 0208 kernel patch causes the scan stall.
+- USER also reports haptics regressed from quick strong buzz to long/weak, then entered fastboot. Captured haptic driver records show drive 0x6a (full DT limit), 30 ms minimum, no capped events. Perceived regression confirmed only by USER; timing/logging effect remains a hypothesis, not a diagnosed cause. Do not increase drive past DT values.
+- Temporarily booted verified 0209 image (SHA256 6cfe48cd8e2734759faac8c7d07e7f56d868ad9a1fe7c138d46570cd14f59ca0): Sending/Booting OKAY. Capture offset work/audio-runtime/0209-wifi-recovery-start.json. Awaiting startup/UTC and Wi-Fi/haptic confirmation.
+- Candidate userspace fix under research: publish bridge hello after verified firmware+transport readiness instead of a completed scan; add a bounded request to cancel an overdue scan, without pretending cancellation succeeded or clearing firmware ownership on a timer. No such fix implemented/built/installed yet.
+- Primary protocol reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.h (wmi_stop_scan_cmd, scan event bits), and wmi-tlv.c serializer. Raw logs/network identifiers remain private outside Git.
+
